WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.920
[tense music playing]

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.880
[breathing heavily]

3
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.400
- You okay. Max?
- Yeah.

4
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.520
[David] Alright.

5
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.400
- [breathing heavily]
- [radio beeps]

6
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:20.920
Ambush.

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.840
<i>We got ambushed over here.</i>

8
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.440
Vehicle's been hit.
Kröller is wounded. Shot to the shoulder.

9
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.880
Alright. men.
Let's get a move on! We have contact!

10
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.120
Send the drones up to locate the shooters.

11
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.640
<i>- We're getting out now.</i>
- Valere!

12
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.200
Let's move out! Now!

13
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.200
[suspenseful music playing]

14
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.120
- Here.
- Thanks.

15
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.320
[grunting]

16
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.040
[David] Alright. Almost.

17
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.720
On the ground. On the ground.

18
00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.240
- [grunting]
- Here.

19
00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:04.760
[drone whirring]

20
00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.480
[suspenseful music continues]

21
00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.840
[Cédric over radio] <i>Eyes in the sky.</i>

22
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.240
It's him. He's gonna kill me.
He's gonna take me out.

23
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.960
[Max] David.

24
00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.880
Who is it?

25
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.440
- Who wants to kill you?
- [Kröller] Let me go and I'll tell you.

26
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.840
[Cédric] Drones at 300 meters.

27
00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.480
We're approaching your position.

28
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

29
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.640
[gunshot]

30
00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.240
[sniper rifle reloads]

31
00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.040
[bullet strikes van]

32
00:01:58.120 --> 00:01:59.880
[reloads rifle]

33
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.120
There's only one shooter.

34
00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:04.480
- Cover me.
- [Max] Copy.

35
00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:07.560
[David] Go.

36
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.880
[gunshots]

37
00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.440
[groans]

38
00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:16.640
[breathes heavily]

39
00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.240
[Max] <i>He's not shooting. I can't find him.</i>

40
00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.480
[Cédric] Drone approaching position.

41
00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.800
[David] <i>Let's go again.</i>

42
00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.880
[suspenseful music continues]

43
00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.320
[gunshots]

44
00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.480
[Max] <i>I can't see him.</i>

45
00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.560
[David] You have a visual on the shooter?

46
00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.960
Negative. No visual.

47
00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.680
[Valère] Converging on target.

48
00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.200
[gunshot]

49
00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.800
[reloads]

50
00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.240
We lost the drone.

51
00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.880
- [gunshot]
- [David] Tango spotted.

52
00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.840
<i>Behind a big rock. Eleven o'clock.</i>

53
00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.160
[gunshots continue]

54
00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.840
[gunshot]

55
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.440
[somber music playing]

56
00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.720
[breathing heavily]

57
00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.520
[Valère] <i>We found the shooter's post.</i>

58
00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:50.480
There's a camo net and casings.
But no one's here.

59
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.840
Kröller's dead.

60
00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.960
<i>- I repeat. Kröller's dead.</i>
- Ah. fuck.

61
00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.280
[pants]

62
00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.920
ELITE FORCE

63
00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.680
[helicopter whirring]

64
00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.760
[officers chattering indistinctly]

65
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.840
We widened out the search area.
but still no sign of the shooter.

66
00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:41.160
What a surprise.

67
00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.040
Did Kröller's wife say anything?

68
00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.280
Recon's with her now but apparently

69
00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.560
she doesn't know that much
about her own husband.

70
00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.320
What are you thinking?

71
00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.800
Same thing you are.

72
00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:02.120
The CL-20. Christophe. now this.

73
00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.240
The shooter was in position
when we came by.

74
00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.240
They're not just professionals.
They know everything about us.

75
00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.240
Yeah. And I can't say I like it.

76
00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.680
The team recovered some ammo casings.
Maybe there's some fingerprints.

77
00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.560
You know they're not gonna find prints.

78
00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.800
[indistinct radio chatter]

79
00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:39.560
[Rapha] It's alright.
No one's accusing you of anything.

80
00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:42.400
We just want to figure out what happened.

81
00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.520
Do you know if your father.
your husband. ma'am.

82
00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:51.080
do you know if he hid anything here?
In the cottage? Or on the grounds?

83
00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.480
[Max] Why are the kids still here?

84
00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:56.440
[Valère] No one to take care of them.
Everyone's hunting for the shooter.

85
00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.240
[Max] Their dad just died.
We can't just leave them here.

86
00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.080
[Valère] So what?

87
00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.800
You volunteering
after the shit you pulled?

88
00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.720
Playing the hero can bite you in the ass.

89
00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:12.040
[poignant music playing]

90
00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.360
Here. You must be starving.

91
00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.120
[camera shutter clicking]

92
00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:33.760
[man] Right there. Another casing.

93
00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.840
[music turns pensive]

94
00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.880
Take the photo. I'll keep searching.

95
00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:40.840
[camera shutter clicking]

96
00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.200
Okay. good. We'll see what we get.

97
00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.200
Okay.

98
00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.080
Some light tracks over here.

99
00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.040
[camera shutter clicking]

100
00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.880
[Max] What the hell?
Stop busting my balls.

101
00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.800
- [Valère] Who do you think you're--
- [Max] You're starting to piss me off.

102
00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.080
I think I'm talking to you.
Just lay off me. come on!

103
00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.120
[Valère] You're not the only one
getting pissed off. I'm not joking.

104
00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.440
- [Max] I don't fucking care!
- [Valère] Smart-ass.

105
00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:18.080
Hey! Come on. stop it!

106
00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.080
Hey. hey. hey!

107
00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.120
[clamoring]

108
00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.240
Enough!

109
00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:27.120
You proud of yourselves?!

110
00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:31.720
Pressure's getting to you?
Well. the pressure's getting to me too!

111
00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.880
We just got a guy killed
who was under our fucking protection!

112
00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.840
And that's never happened to us before!

113
00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.640
[tense music playing]

114
00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:45.080
But if you're incapable of dealing with
the stress. then do us a favor and quit.

115
00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.320
You mad? Go to the gym
and find yourself a punching bag.

116
00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:50.960
Is that clear?

117
00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.080
I said. is that clear?!

118
00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.320
Yeah.

119
00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.600
[music fades]

120
00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.640
[metal tool clatters]

121
00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.680
TECHNICAL ROOM

122
00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:26.720
[device beeps]

123
00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.760
[suspenseful music playing]

124
00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.720
14.98.

125
00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:53.680
Yeah.

126
00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.120
[computer beeps]

127
00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:21.320
MEASURING

128
00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:26.320
[whirring]

129
00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.640
[cell phone buzzing]

130
00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:45.880
Yeah. Céline?

131
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.240
We need you here.

132
00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:49.760
<i>He's awake.</i>

133
00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.720
[medical devices beeping]

134
00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:07.880
I knew you were gonna wake up.

135
00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.080
Hmm.

136
00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:11.160
[poignant music playing]

137
00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.240
Don't worry. Christophe.

138
00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.240
I'll get you some makeup.
No one'll notice a thing.

139
00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.320
[chuckles weakly]

140
00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:34.720
[Christophe groans]

141
00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.840
Any idea who did this to you?

142
00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:45.800
[exhales]

143
00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:52.400
I'm gonna find them.

144
00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:58.680
I promise.

145
00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:04.600
[Max] It's just the three pages
so not a long read.

146
00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.640
But if you don't mind.
I. uh… I wanna know what you think.

147
00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.120
{\an8}LAURENT VILLIERS.
LIEUTENANT KILLED IN ACTIVE DUTY

148
00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.480
[soft jazz music playing over speakers]

149
00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:15.640
Here you go.

150
00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:17.840
- The chef's special. madam.
- Wow.

151
00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:20.120
At the very least.
it'll fill us up before the party.

152
00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.920
My dad's recipe.

153
00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.120
What do you think?

154
00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:26.360
What I find weird is that

155
00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:30.480
the only one who was with your dad
when he died was David.

156
00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.880
So where's his statement?

157
00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.320
[Max] Yeah. I don't get that either.

158
00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.880
Why wasn't it archived?

159
00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.680
That's what I'm gonna find out.

160
00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:47.800
[upbeat music playing in the distance]

161
00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:50.480
- A bit basic.
- Really? Basic?

162
00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.840
- Hey! How are you?
- Hey. what's up? Not at your internship?

163
00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.280
- You good?
- Yeah. you?

164
00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.760
["Sugabby" by Sad Night Dynamite
playing over speakers]

165
00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:03.080
<i>♪ Goes to Cash App</i>
<i>Daddy transferred her a grand ♪</i>

166
00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.160
<i>♪ Life's sweet for the sugar babies… ♪</i>

167
00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.200
Hey!

168
00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:10.000
- Thanks.
- Hi. David. it's great to see you.

169
00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:14.280
- [David] Happy birthday. bro.
- You alright?

170
00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:16.760
So tell me. How's he doing? You see him?

171
00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:20.480
He's okay. Recovering. Slowly.

172
00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.760
[Cédric] Hey. everyone! Excuse me!
Two seconds. okay?

173
00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:26.320
Hang on! Valère.
turn the music down a bit. would you?

174
00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.880
I won't be long.
I swear. I just wanna say two words.

175
00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:30.920
- [music stops]
- To Christophe!

176
00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.520
[all] To Christophe!

177
00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:35.520
[cheering and whooping]

178
00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:40.920
Now let's have some fun. alright?

179
00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.240
[man] Yeah!

180
00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.560
[music resumes]

181
00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:45.960
Well. cheers.

182
00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:47.880
[laughing]

183
00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:50.600
What a fuckin' dickhead. Valère. Fuck.

184
00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:56.920
Hey. I'd never say this to them
but the new guys are fire!

185
00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:58.920
You're not wrong.

186
00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:01.680
You alright?

187
00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.760
I mean. at home with Jess.
Everything okay?

188
00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:08.680
Yeah. It's fine. Smooth.

189
00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:11.200
- Smooth.
- And she's got work.

190
00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:13.840
Yeah. She's got a lot of work.

191
00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.520
- You wanna stop doing that?
- What?

192
00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:19.960
Your little negotiator tactic.

193
00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:22.640
Repeating my sentences back to me
to get me to talk like I'm insane.

194
00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:26.360
No way. man. At least insane guys
say something to say. you know?

195
00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.160
Look. I know I'm drunk
but I gotta say this.

196
00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.360
Ah. fucking hell.
You've fallen in love with me?

197
00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:35.200
No. Fuck you. man. alright?
I'm being serious here.

198
00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:40.600
But if you ever need to talk about Jess
or anything… Uh. I'm here. Right?

199
00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:41.760
I know.

200
00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.760
[lively dance music playing over speakers]

201
00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:50.480
[laughs]

202
00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:53.000
[cheering]

203
00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:56.680
Yeah!

204
00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.880
[Rapha laughing]

205
00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:10.240
{\an8}MISSED CALL MANON

206
00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:24.160
<i>Hey. this is Manon's voicemail.</i>
<i>If I didn't pick up.</i>

207
00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.080
<i>it's 'cause I didn't feel like it.</i>

208
00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:39.160
<i>Hi. it's Jess.</i>
<i>Leave a message after the beep.</i>

209
00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:45.240
[tense music playing]

210
00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:46.200
[man] <i>Go ahead. sir.</i>

211
00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:49.400
[David] I need a favor.
I need you to trace my daughter's number.

212
00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:51.840
- [man] <i>Yeah. No problem. sir.</i>
- [David] Thanks.

213
00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:17.080
[music fades]

214
00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:19.880
- [man] <i>It's coming from the same address.</i>
- Thanks.

215
00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:22.360
[bike engine powers down]

216
00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:24.440
[techno music playing distantly]

217
00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.000
[techno music continues over speakers]

218
00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:00.200
[sniffing]

219
00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:10.480
[techno music continues]

220
00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:13.600
[crowd whooping and chattering]

221
00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.280
[speaking indistinctly]

222
00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:41.240
- [techno music continues]
- [people whooping]

223
00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:02.160
We're leaving. Let's go!

224
00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:03.440
What are you doing here?

225
00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.600
- Hey! Hey! She's not going anywhere!
- Hey! Stop! Stop it!

226
00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:08.400
- Let him go!
- Ah!

227
00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.280
- What are you doing?
- You wanna fucking go?

228
00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:11.760
You don't have to hurt them!

229
00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:12.880
[yells]

230
00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:15.240
- Sorry! I'm sorry!
- Move.

231
00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:18.040
Out of my way.

232
00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:20.240
- [Manon screams]
- [bottle shatters]

233
00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:21.160
[music stops]

234
00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:23.280
- [groans]
- Stop!

235
00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:26.400
- [nervous chatter]
- [young man] We've gotta do something!

236
00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.720
[grunts]

237
00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:29.480
[clamoring]

238
00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:30.800
[Manon] Get off of him!

239
00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:32.000
- No. don't!
- [grunts]

240
00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:33.680
Dad. stop it!

241
00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:34.720
[taser crackles]

242
00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:35.760
[Manon] Dad!

243
00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:37.240
[grunting]

244
00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:40.120
- Hey! Get the hell outta here!
- [women scream]

245
00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:43.000
- [taser crackles]
- Let him go! Stop it! Dad!

246
00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.760
[women clamoring]

247
00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:46.200
[thuds]

248
00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:48.040
[partygoers murmuring]

249
00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:49.280
Let's go.

250
00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:50.880
Okay. Shit.

251
00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.640
What the hell's your problem?

252
00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:54.680
[David] What's my problem?
What's your problem?

253
00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:56.800
I'm obviously
missing something here. Manon.

254
00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.320
- You sneak out. call me 15 times--
- What are you talking about?

255
00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:02.880
I missed a bunch of calls from your phone!
When I call you back. you don't pick up.

256
00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:06.360
When I come to find you. you're at a rave?
And you're asking what my problem is?

257
00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:08.200
[man] We're gonna call the police!

258
00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:12.000
Oh yeah? You wanna call the police?
I've got good news for you.

259
00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.240
I am the fuckin' police!

260
00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:15.680
You made your point. can we go?
Everyone gets it!

261
00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:17.720
- Out.
- You put me in deep shit now. Thanks.

262
00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:20.720
I put you in deep shit?
I miss 15 calls from you. that's my fault?

263
00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:23.120
- What the hell was that about?
- I have no idea what happened.

264
00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.920
I must've pocket dialed you.

265
00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:26.840
Fine. They were pocket dials.

266
00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:29.920
I come and find you at a rave
where everyone's high and wasted.

267
00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.560
Taking MDMA. coke.
speed and who knows what else.

268
00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:35.360
- For fuck's sake. Manon. you're 16.
- Do you think I took any of that?

269
00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:37.720
- I hope not.
- I didn't.

270
00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.640
I just came to hang out with my friends.

271
00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.120
Without telling us?

272
00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.880
- Who would I tell?
- I don't know. maybe your Mum and Dad?

273
00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:46.400
Mom's out for dinner with her friends
and you're never around!

274
00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.480
You think I haven't done this before?

275
00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:52.560
I don't know.

276
00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:55.760
Maybe if you were around more. you would.

277
00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:59.120
Come on. Let's go.

278
00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:06.440
You pulled a Bruce Lee. apparently.

279
00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:10.400
You'd have done so much worse
if you'd been in my shoes.

280
00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:12.000
Hm.

281
00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:15.520
- This is great.
- Not bad. huh?

282
00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:17.400
- Yeah.
- It's a company gift.

283
00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:18.920
For the new job.

284
00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:30.880
I wanted to tell you that. um…

285
00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:34.240
I wanted to tell you
how much I admire you.

286
00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:36.520
Always have.

287
00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:41.160
You deserve… everything you've worked for.

288
00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:42.960
And Manon's so talented.

289
00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:45.800
She deserves better teachers
than what she can get here.

290
00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:51.840
But. um…

291
00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:55.920
If I'm being completely honest. I…

292
00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.000
[gentle music playing]

293
00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.640
I want you to stay.

294
00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:03.720
[sighs]

295
00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:10.720
Is there anything I can do
to convince you?

296
00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:14.960
I don't know.

297
00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:20.640
[indistinct radio chatter]

298
00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:23.200
- No. they said it was quiet yesterday.
- That’s good.

299
00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:25.280
[both grunting]

300
00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:28.000
Right. Send it back right away.

301
00:20:29.840 --> 00:20:30.920
[grunting]

302
00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.320
Keep your guard up.
Even when you're striking.

303
00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:36.720
[tense music playing]

304
00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:59.040
[door opens]

305
00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:03.760
- My report on the Kröller mission.
- Stick around.

306
00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:15.360
What're you working on?

307
00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:19.160
Hey.

308
00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:26.480
You're trying to identify some ammo?

309
00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:28.680
[turns pages]

310
00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:39.600
Okay.

311
00:21:42.680 --> 00:21:44.320
- Need some help?
- No.

312
00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:49.240
You know I was at
weapon control before joining?

313
00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:52.080
No. Guess you don't.

314
00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:55.920
You know. even geniuses like you
could use help sometimes.

315
00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:09.600
12-7 NATO.

316
00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:11.640
[pensive music playing]

317
00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:14.360
But it's not standard issue.
Where'd you get it?

318
00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:19.560
I bet it's not
in the manufacturer's database.

319
00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:24.720
And the serial number can't be traced.
Otherwise. it would've been.

320
00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:31.840
You're wasting my time. Max. We done here?

321
00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:38.920
This is specialized ammo
made by the military.

322
00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:43.280
How could you possibly know that?

323
00:22:43.360 --> 00:22:46.280
The army stopped making
their ammo a decade ago.

324
00:22:46.840 --> 00:22:49.800
They only produced a small quantity
of these for research in weapons labs.

325
00:22:50.400 --> 00:22:51.920
Wait. weapons labs?

326
00:22:52.680 --> 00:22:56.160
Yeah. They took them out of circulation.
That's why it can't be traced.

327
00:22:56.960 --> 00:22:57.800
You're sure?

328
00:22:58.400 --> 00:22:59.720
Mm-hmm.

329
00:23:05.240 --> 00:23:07.440
- Where you going?
- To see Christophe.

330
00:23:07.520 --> 00:23:08.680
[Max] I'll come with.

331
00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:16.720
[indistinct chatter]

332
00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:39.920
Yes. that's good.

333
00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:42.360
Yeah. very good.

334
00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:47.800
Why'd they bring me that?

335
00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:51.880
Excuse me. guys.
I didn't ask for a respirator.

336
00:23:51.960 --> 00:23:54.120
- [nurse] Can I help you?
- We're here to visit our friend.

337
00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:55.320
[nurse] Of course. go ahead.

338
00:23:55.400 --> 00:23:57.880
[doctor] Hey. I'm talking to you!
Excuse me?

339
00:23:57.960 --> 00:23:59.360
Come on. seriously?

340
00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:00.520
Hey!

341
00:24:01.560 --> 00:24:04.080
- It's one thing after another here.
- [David] What's going on?

342
00:24:04.160 --> 00:24:06.200
[doctor] I didn't ask for a respirator.

343
00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:07.600
- Excuse me.
- [nurse] Yes. Doctor?

344
00:24:07.680 --> 00:24:09.840
I need to know
who's in charge of equipment.

345
00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:11.200
I didn't order that.

346
00:24:18.440 --> 00:24:19.480
[dramatic music playing]

347
00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:20.920
[David] Holy shit.

348
00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:24.400
We have to evacuate right now.
There's a bomb!

349
00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:26.240
I'll take care of it.
Go do it right now. Go.

350
00:24:27.480 --> 00:24:29.160
Okay. Get Tanya on the phone. now!

351
00:24:29.240 --> 00:24:31.560
[suspenseful music playing]

352
00:24:36.440 --> 00:24:37.960
Are you cold? You want your scarf?

353
00:24:38.040 --> 00:24:38.960
No.

354
00:24:39.800 --> 00:24:41.480
[cell phone ringing]

355
00:24:42.000 --> 00:24:43.040
- Hello?
- [Max] <i>Tanya?</i>

356
00:24:43.120 --> 00:24:44.880
It's Max. I'm at the hospital with David.

357
00:24:44.960 --> 00:24:46.800
<i>Christophe's room</i>
<i>was rigged with explosives.</i>

358
00:24:46.880 --> 00:24:49.680
<i>- Have you evacuated the building?</i>
- [Max] It's in progress.

359
00:24:49.760 --> 00:24:51.560
- Can I video call you?
<i>- No.</i>

360
00:24:51.640 --> 00:24:52.880
No. absolutely not.

361
00:24:52.960 --> 00:24:55.920
Just put me on speaker and move
the phone away to avoid interference.

362
00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:56.840
Okay.

363
00:24:59.800 --> 00:25:02.280
- [Tanya] <i>Can you hear me?</i>
- [Max] Yeah. I hear you!

364
00:25:02.360 --> 00:25:03.400
<i>Tell me what you're seeing.</i>

365
00:25:03.480 --> 00:25:07.040
There's. uh… There's six tubes of CL-20.

366
00:25:07.120 --> 00:25:08.720
There's wires connected inside the cart.

367
00:25:08.800 --> 00:25:11.560
And it's. uh…
It's in a cart like in the O.R.

368
00:25:11.640 --> 00:25:12.720
<i>The first thing is.</i>

369
00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:14.600
make sure the cart won't trip anything.

370
00:25:14.680 --> 00:25:17.200
<i>Look everywhere. Around it. underneath it.</i>

371
00:25:18.880 --> 00:25:21.080
- [gunshots]
- [staff screaming]

372
00:25:21.160 --> 00:25:22.280
[gunshot]

373
00:25:24.560 --> 00:25:25.640
[Tanya] <i>Anything. Max?</i>

374
00:25:26.480 --> 00:25:28.400
<i>- Max?</i>
- [Max] <i>No. we're good.</i>

375
00:25:28.480 --> 00:25:30.520
- [Tanya] <i>Follow the cable harness.</i>
- [Max] <i>Okay.</i>

376
00:25:30.600 --> 00:25:33.480
[David] We're evacuating the hospital!
Everyone out. now!

377
00:25:34.520 --> 00:25:37.240
Excuse me. sir?
We have to get you out of here.

378
00:25:37.320 --> 00:25:40.360
- [nurse] We need you in pediatrics!
- [doctor] Yeah. I'm coming. Coming!

379
00:25:40.440 --> 00:25:41.880
Find me the chart-- Oh!

380
00:25:41.960 --> 00:25:44.600
[alarm blaring]

381
00:25:45.240 --> 00:25:48.200
There's. um… There's a plate
that's blocking me from getting in.

382
00:25:48.280 --> 00:25:49.320
I have to open it.

383
00:25:49.400 --> 00:25:50.680
No. no. no. Leave the plate.

384
00:25:50.760 --> 00:25:53.920
You check that the plate
has no wires coming off of it first.

385
00:25:56.160 --> 00:25:57.480
- [alarm blaring]
- You okay?

386
00:25:57.560 --> 00:25:59.560
[suspenseful music continues]

387
00:26:00.840 --> 00:26:03.240
[Tanya] <i>So then you're going</i>
<i>to remove it very gently. okay?</i>

388
00:26:03.320 --> 00:26:06.840
<i>- Don't take any chances.</i>
- Just a minute. Okay.

389
00:26:07.440 --> 00:26:10.480
{\an8}<i>- You still with me?</i>
- Yeah. I hear you. Yeah.

390
00:26:12.720 --> 00:26:14.600
[distant gunshots]

391
00:26:14.680 --> 00:26:15.840
[people screaming]

392
00:26:15.920 --> 00:26:17.760
- [indistinct yelling]
- [woman] Help!

393
00:26:18.840 --> 00:26:21.200
[suspenseful music continues]

394
00:26:21.280 --> 00:26:22.120
All right.

395
00:26:25.760 --> 00:26:27.040
Okay. I got it open.

396
00:26:27.840 --> 00:26:29.040
[Tanya] <i>What do you see?</i>

397
00:26:29.120 --> 00:26:32.240
[Max] <i>There's 12 more tubes of CL-20.</i>
<i>a detonator and a timer.</i>

398
00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:33.720
[Tanya] <i>How much time left?</i>

399
00:26:35.200 --> 00:26:36.520
Three minutes. 30.

400
00:26:37.120 --> 00:26:38.800
[Tanya] <i>Find the live wire and cut it.</i>

401
00:26:38.880 --> 00:26:39.840
Okay.

402
00:26:40.480 --> 00:26:41.600
I can't see a thing.

403
00:26:42.400 --> 00:26:43.680
Max. do you read me?

404
00:26:44.320 --> 00:26:45.160
Max. come in!

405
00:26:46.520 --> 00:26:47.760
Okay.

406
00:26:53.280 --> 00:26:55.040
Police! You seen anyone?

407
00:26:55.120 --> 00:26:56.880
[man] There's a man in scrubs.
He's got a gun!

408
00:26:56.960 --> 00:26:58.880
- Where is he?
- I don't know where he went.

409
00:26:58.960 --> 00:27:00.040
He was shooting!

410
00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:01.880
I need you to move.

411
00:27:01.960 --> 00:27:03.960
[suspenseful music continues]

412
00:27:15.520 --> 00:27:17.640
I'm with the police. I need you to move!

413
00:27:24.840 --> 00:27:26.320
Freeze!

414
00:27:26.400 --> 00:27:29.240
Put your weapon on the ground!
Do it slowly.

415
00:27:31.560 --> 00:27:32.720
Hands above your head!

416
00:27:37.800 --> 00:27:39.000
[car tires screeching]

417
00:27:39.080 --> 00:27:39.960
[gunshots]

418
00:27:40.040 --> 00:27:42.200
[intense music playing]

419
00:27:44.080 --> 00:27:46.760
Max! What's your status?

420
00:27:59.640 --> 00:28:01.200
[screeching]

421
00:28:07.640 --> 00:28:09.560
[gunshots]

422
00:28:23.920 --> 00:28:25.280
[gunfire]

423
00:28:32.520 --> 00:28:33.960
[suspenseful music playing]

424
00:28:34.560 --> 00:28:36.160
- [Tanya] <i>You still with me?</i>
- Yeah.

425
00:28:37.880 --> 00:28:39.800
- Pretty sure I got it.
- How are you gonna cut it?

426
00:28:40.400 --> 00:28:41.600
Uh…

427
00:28:42.440 --> 00:28:44.200
[Tanya] <i>And make sure</i>
<i>there's only one wire</i>

428
00:28:44.280 --> 00:28:47.000
<i>connecting the detonator to the CL-20.</i>

429
00:28:52.080 --> 00:28:54.000
- [gunshots]
- Let's get outta here!

430
00:28:59.080 --> 00:29:00.280
[tires screeching]

431
00:29:03.560 --> 00:29:05.880
[intense music playing]

432
00:29:15.960 --> 00:29:17.400
- We've got a problem.
- [Tanya] <i>What?</i>

433
00:29:17.480 --> 00:29:20.120
There's a wire connected
to a second trigger.

434
00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:21.680
<i>Can you access that one?</i>

435
00:29:21.760 --> 00:29:23.280
[suspenseful music playing]

436
00:29:25.440 --> 00:29:26.760
It's on the other side.

437
00:29:26.840 --> 00:29:29.040
Can you cut both wires at the same time?

438
00:29:29.120 --> 00:29:30.280
Oh. fuck.

439
00:29:32.400 --> 00:29:34.600
[intense music playing]

440
00:29:45.280 --> 00:29:47.280
[suspenseful music playing]

441
00:29:53.480 --> 00:29:55.480
[tires screech]

442
00:29:58.240 --> 00:29:59.400
[gunshot]

443
00:30:05.040 --> 00:30:06.560
[Tanya] <i>Max. you there?</i>

444
00:30:06.640 --> 00:30:07.480
[sighs]

445
00:30:09.640 --> 00:30:11.120
[Max] <i>No. I can't. Dammit.</i>

446
00:30:13.840 --> 00:30:15.160
<i>I can't cut both at the same time.</i>

447
00:30:15.240 --> 00:30:17.400
- Max!
- [Tanya] <i>Just get out of there. now!</i>

448
00:30:17.480 --> 00:30:19.000
<i>You still have time! Move!</i>

449
00:30:19.080 --> 00:30:21.600
[breathing heavily]

450
00:30:21.680 --> 00:30:23.320
- [David] <i>Max!</i>
- I'm not leaving. I can't.

451
00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:26.040
If you can hear me. don't take any risks!
I'm coming!

452
00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:29.760
[Tanya] <i>Max. Get out of there!</i>

453
00:30:29.840 --> 00:30:31.080
[Max] <i>I can do this.</i>

454
00:30:31.160 --> 00:30:32.880
[suspenseful music playing]

455
00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:44.760
Tell me what you need.

456
00:30:47.080 --> 00:30:48.360
[Max] Grab the scissors.

457
00:30:48.880 --> 00:30:50.600
You can't see me.
so you'll have to listen.

458
00:30:50.680 --> 00:30:51.520
Yeah.

459
00:30:51.600 --> 00:30:53.760
There's two detonators.
One on your side and one on mine.

460
00:30:53.840 --> 00:30:55.640
We're gonna have
to cut them at the same time.

461
00:30:55.720 --> 00:30:57.160
- Okay.
- There are two wires.

462
00:30:57.240 --> 00:30:58.800
The one you want is on the right.

463
00:30:58.880 --> 00:31:01.000
- Your right or my right?
- Your right.

464
00:31:02.480 --> 00:31:03.320
Okay.

465
00:31:03.400 --> 00:31:05.400
[suspenseful music continues]

466
00:31:06.600 --> 00:31:07.640
Shit.

467
00:31:10.280 --> 00:31:12.280
- How much time?
- 40 seconds.

468
00:31:13.840 --> 00:31:14.840
[David] Fuck.

469
00:31:15.560 --> 00:31:18.440
- I can't-- I can't see anything.
- It'll be fine. I can guide you.

470
00:31:18.520 --> 00:31:20.880
<i>Bring the scissors closer to me slowly.</i>

471
00:31:22.920 --> 00:31:24.520
And a little bit more to the right.

472
00:31:25.760 --> 00:31:26.920
Good. Forward.

473
00:31:29.440 --> 00:31:31.040
Forward just a bit more.

474
00:31:31.120 --> 00:31:33.080
[music intensifies]

475
00:31:33.160 --> 00:31:35.840
Yeah. there. That's it.
Stop moving. Don't move.

476
00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:38.480
<i>We cut on three.</i>

477
00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:39.800
<i>Okay?</i>

478
00:31:40.360 --> 00:31:43.400
One. Two. Three.

479
00:31:48.360 --> 00:31:50.960
- [David exhales]
- [music calms]

480
00:31:51.040 --> 00:31:52.440
[tools clatter]

481
00:31:53.120 --> 00:31:54.160
[exhales]

482
00:31:54.240 --> 00:31:56.240
[panting]

483
00:32:06.360 --> 00:32:07.480
[exhales]

484
00:32:12.920 --> 00:32:14.840
You okay. honey? Yeah. you're okay.

485
00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:17.160
[Tanya sighs]

486
00:32:19.240 --> 00:32:21.000
Son of a bitch.

487
00:32:21.080 --> 00:32:22.680
I'll go tell the others.

488
00:32:25.720 --> 00:32:26.720
[coughs]

489
00:32:35.880 --> 00:32:37.040
[exhales]

490
00:32:37.120 --> 00:32:38.160
[chuckles]

491
00:32:44.040 --> 00:32:45.560
I guess we live to fight another day.

492
00:32:46.760 --> 00:32:47.720
[sighs]

493
00:32:48.920 --> 00:32:49.840
[coughs]

494
00:32:51.520 --> 00:32:52.520
[sighs]

495
00:32:54.160 --> 00:32:56.160
You remember the lab where Laurent died?

496
00:32:57.160 --> 00:32:59.160
[solemn music playing]

497
00:33:03.800 --> 00:33:07.120
I think the guy who planted the bomb
is the guy you dragged outside.

498
00:33:20.600 --> 00:33:22.480
So it's revenge.

499
00:33:24.960 --> 00:33:26.200
That's what I think.

500
00:33:30.120 --> 00:33:32.000
It's my fault.

501
00:33:33.000 --> 00:33:34.840
[David] No. It was a mistake.

502
00:33:37.560 --> 00:33:39.680
We all made mistakes that day.

503
00:33:44.040 --> 00:33:45.080
[groans]

504
00:33:51.760 --> 00:33:54.400
David. you can't outrun the past.

505
00:34:09.160 --> 00:34:10.480
Just look.

506
00:34:12.360 --> 00:34:13.600
